Adaptive cadence: 0098's settle after a 3 -> 2 (missed slots in its first 300 ms not counted) was kept through 1X.
CadenceController's two_from_three_ was cleared by a move up, a scene change, a start and a stop, but not by entering
or leaving 1X, so after 3 -> 2 -> 1X -> 2 the first 300 ms of the 2 that 1X left for still ignored missed slots, as if
it came from 3 (native review, round 5). Now entering 1X and leaving it clear it: a 2 entered from 1X counts its missed
slots from the start, as before 0098. New test cadence_3x_exit_after_one_tests (latency_control_tests): fails before
(still at 2, 266 ms after the return, two episodes in), passes after (3 at 177 ms).

